{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.663,
   "text": "My grandmother's farm had an old stone well, sealed under a heavy wooden lid."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.263,
   "end": 11.78,
   "text": "She had one rule about it."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 12.58,
   "end": 18.916,
   "text": "Never drop anything down that well after dark. And if something ever comes back up... don't touch it."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 19.516,
   "end": 24.124,
   "text": "The summer I stayed with her, I broke that rule on my very first night."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 24.724,
   "end": 29.673,
   "text": "I slipped a penny through a crack in the lid... and wished for someone to play with."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.473,
   "end": 32.671,
   "text": "I never heard it land."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 34.671,
   "end": 38.98,
   "text": "The next morning, there was a penny on my pillow. Cold... and wet."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 39.78,
   "end": 44.943,
   "text": "Grandma went pale. She said, from now on, you stay inside after sunset."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 45.543,
   "end": 49.447,
   "text": "So every night, I watched the well from my bedroom window."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 50.247,
   "end": 53.724,
   "text": "On the last night of summer... the lid slid open."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 55.924,
   "end": 59.764,
   "text": "Then something tapped on my window. Three soft taps."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 62.364,
   "end": 67.463,
   "text": "And a voice, exactly like mine, whispered... let me in. I'm what you wished for."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 68.863,
   "end": 75.583,
   "text": "Mom came to get me the next morning. She hugged us both... and she doesn't remember ever having just one kid."
  }
 ],
